%S A401449 2170,3281,4392,5607,6718,7829,32780,43891,56108,67219,327804,438915,
%T A401449 561084,672195,1107509,3278044,4388890,4389155,5610844,5611109,
%U A401449 6721955,8892490,11074890,11074906,32780444,43889093,43889109,43891555,56108444,56110890,56110906
%N A401449 Non-repdigit positive integers whose proper decimal prefixes and proper decimal suffixes have equal sums.
%C A401449 Suffixes are read as numbers, so leading zeros are ignored, e.g., 07509 counts as 7509.
%C A401449 Repdigits are excluded because they always satisfy the condition.
%C A401449 A digit c can be appended to a term m to give another term only when c = (digit sum of m)/(number of digits of m) is an integer. Then appending any number of copies of c also gives terms.
%H A401449 Karan Sharma, <a href="/A401449/b401449.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..88</a>
%e A401449 2170 is a term since its proper prefixes and proper suffixes have equal sums:
%e A401449 217 + 21 + 2 = 170 + 70 + 0 = 240.
%e A401449 32780 is a term since 3278 + 327 + 32 + 3 = 2780 + 780 + 80 + 0 = 3640.
%o A401449 (Python)
%o A401449 def ok(m):
%o A401449     s = str(m)
%o A401449     if len(set(s)) == 1: return False
%o A401449     return sum(int(s[:k]) for k in range(1, len(s))) == sum(int(s[k:]) for k in range(1, len(s)))
%o A401449 print([m for m in range(1, 10**6) if ok(m)]) # _Karan Sharma_, Oct 25 2026
%Y A401449 Cf. A010785.
%K A401449 nonn,base,new
